PART OF CANVAS
--------------

The Canvas web user interface, served by canvas-server.

This repository is one component of the Canvas project. It is developed and
released as part of Canvas, but it lives in its own repository:

    this component   https://github.com/canvas-ui/canvas-web
    the project      https://github.com/canvas-ui/canvas-server

Canvas components are not all licensed the same way. The server runtime and the
services it embeds are dual-licensed. The standalone clients are AGPL-only. The
COMPONENTS section of the project NOTICE lists which is which.

NETWORK USE
-----------

This component is served to users over a network, which is the situation section
13 of the AGPL addresses. If you run a modified version and let users interact
with it, whether those users are customers, the public or anyone else who is not
you, they must be able to obtain the corresponding source of your modified
version.

canvas-server publishes that source information for the interface to use. It
sets an `X-Source-Code` header on every response, and `GET /rest/v2/ping` (no
authentication required) reports the running version, revision and source URL.
If you deploy a modified version, repoint these at the repository that publishes
your changes, using `CANVAS_SOURCE_URL` and `CANVAS_SOURCE_COMMIT`. Removing
them instead of repointing them does not satisfy the licence.

